<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fuad Stephens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/1976">1976</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Donald Stephens, Tun Fuad Stephens</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fuad Stephens, born Donald Stephens, was a journalist and Kadazan leader in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> who founded the United National Kadazan Organisation. He helped bring the colony into Malaysia in 1963 as the state of Sabah and served as its first chief minister. He became chief minister again in 1976 but died weeks later in an air crash.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fuad-stephens.jpg" alt="Fuad Stephens" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tun_Fuad_Stephens.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
